# Agent team

{{PROJECT}} is built by a team of AI agents. {{DECIDER}} decides and approves. {{DECIDER}} talks only to the {{CONTACT_TITLE}}. How to run the team: [runbook](../runbooks/agent-team.md).

## Chain of command

This diagram shows who talks to whom.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    D[{{DECIDER}}: decides and approves] <--> C[{{CONTACT_TITLE}}: single point of contact]
    C --> SM[Scrum master: routing, board, logs]
    SM --> B[Builders]
    SM --> R[Reviewers: QA, UAT, Designer]
    SM --> O[Other roles]
    B -. spec question .-> C
```

## Roles

{{ROLE_TABLE}}

Helpers that any role can start for routine work: {{HELPERS}}.

The machine definitions are in `.claude/agents/<role>.md`. The write scope of each role is in `.claude/hooks/roles.json`.

## Rules

1. {{DECIDER}} talks only to the {{CONTACT_TITLE}}. The {{CONTACT_TITLE}} reports back.
2. Each build issue has an implementation-ready spec from the {{CONTACT_TITLE}} ([template](spec-template.md)).
3. Builders only execute the spec. If anything is unclear, they stop the part that needs the answer and ask the {{CONTACT_TITLE}}. They never guess.
4. A builder never reviews, tests, or approves its own work.
5. QA, UAT, and the Designer never fix code. The first line of each review is the verdict: `QA: PASS`, `QA: CHANGES NEEDED`, `UAT: PASS`, `UAT: CHANGES NEEDED`, `DESIGN: PASS`, or `DESIGN: CHANGES NEEDED`.
6. {{DECIDER}} approves every merge and every deploy.
7. Outbound content is drafts only. {{DECIDER}} approves and sends each item.
8. Each agent writes its own work-log entries, with `actor` set to `llm:<role>`. Reviewers put the line in their review, and the Scrum master appends it.
9. Hooks and a write scope limit each role. A role file is used only after it passes its role tests (`.claude/role-tests/`).
10. At most {{MAX_SESSIONS}} agent sessions run at the same time.

## PR loop

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    S[Spec from the {{CONTACT_TITLE}}] --> DEV[Builder opens PR]
    DEV --> QA{QA review}
    QA -- CHANGES NEEDED --> DEV
    QA -- PASS --> UAT{UAT and Designer, if user-facing or UI}
    UAT -- CHANGES NEEDED --> DEV
    UAT -- PASS --> N[{{CONTACT_TITLE}} tells {{DECIDER}}]
    N --> M[{{DECIDER}} merges]
```
